# Build context for src/Keyloop.ServiceScheduler.Api/Dockerfile (context: the repository root). Allow-list: only the shared build
# settings and the API with its referenced projects are sent, never node_modules, test output or local secrets.
*
!global.json
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!.editorconfig
!src/Keyloop.ServiceScheduler.ServiceDefaults/
!src/Keyloop.ServiceScheduler.Domain/
!src/Keyloop.ServiceScheduler.Infrastructure/
!src/Keyloop.ServiceScheduler.Api/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/appsettings.*.local.json
# Credential files a developer may keep inside the allowed projects. The allow-list above would send them; these lines win
# because they come later. BuildKit reads this file, not the root .dockerignore, when the build names this Dockerfile.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.npmrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/secrets.json
